zombies snowmen giant snakes and the  worst cgi you've ever seen think you  loved these movies think again  washington irving's classic horror story  the legend of sleepy hollow has been  adapted to the screen numerous times one  of the most notable iterations is tim  burton's 1999 film sleepy hollow  starring the director's most frequent  collaborator johnny depp as ichabod  crane fans of burton who grew up  familiar with this revered gothic style  were eager to see him try his hand at an  r-rated horror film and he's certainly  delivered upon the movie's tagline heads  will roll  clean as dandelion heads apparently  despite triumph at the box office  generally positive reviews from critics  and three academy award nominations the  movie seemed to disappear into the fog  following its release sleepy hollow  remains a visually stunning achievement  and it certainly has its fans but it has  failed to garner any kind of enduring  fandom nowadays it has mostly been  forgotten  from the tornadoes of twister to the  eruptions of dante's peak planetary  seemed to be under constant assault in  1990 cinema the disaster genre is rife  with unforgettable scenes of nature's  fury and destruction but mimi leather's  comet-based action thriller deep impact  sadly imploded before it could really  get going deep impact actually enjoyed  some early success at the start of the  summer of 98 but then a month later the  unthinkable happened armageddon although  critics were harsher on michael bay's  movie it's outshined deep impact in two  key ways it had more consistent action  set pieces with stronger production  value and it featured stronger more  memorable characters the only enduring  action and deep impact arrives late in  the final act when a comet strikes the  atlantic ocean and triggers an enormous  tidal wave this leads to the movie's  most famous sequence in which new york  city is swallowed by the terrifying  tsunami unfortunately everything before  the comet's arrival is a bit of a slug  deep impact features unnecessarily large  ensemble casts occupying fractured  storylines and none of them are really  compelling enough to stand on their own  the recipient of six razzie nominations  including worst couple for jon voight  and an animatronic snake anaconda is  something of a notorious legend in  hollywood history jennifer lopez icecube  and owen wilson star as members of a  film crew shooting a documentary about a  lost tribe in the amazon they cross  paths with a snake hunter who offers to  help them but instead takes some hostage  and hoodwinks them into helping him  track down a legendary enormous green  anaconda that lives deep in the jungle  dismal reviews from critics didn't  hinder the film's performance at the box  office likely fueled by word of mouth  regarding its status as a so bad as good  classic and it's a laugh at times a  comically large sometimes animatronic  sometimes cgi anaconda is vindictive to  the point of pettiness screeching like a  pterodactyl as it plucks off the crew  one by one while these scenes are  genuinely hilarious however the  remainder of the movie is a snooze voigt  is the only actor who seems to have  understood the assignment whereas the  rest of the cast plays the bonkers  script way too seriously there's a devil  inside everyone  everyone waited with baited breath to  see how alicia silverstone would follow  up her performance in clueless arguably  one of the best high school movies of  all time as such it was no surprise that  excess baggage caved under these  unreasonably high expectations although  the movie notoriously bombed the box  office and in critics estimations it  remained popular among silverstone  die-hards who were thrilled to see the  actor try her hand at a more dramatic  turn still not even that could prevent  this tonally uneven formulated crime  comedy from becoming a forgotten relic  of the 1990s  the christmas genre is chock full of  movies that viewers come back to year  after year unfortunately troy miller's  1998 family fantasy jack frost failed to  secure a spot in the pantheon of holiday  movies perhaps the movie's fatal flaw is  that jack frost begins with the grim  death of a semi-absent father setting a  fairly morbid somber tone from the start  not only suffocates the story as it  trudges on the father spirit returns in  the form of a live-speaking snowman and  tries to reconnect with his troubled son  things just keep getting creepier from  there as the movie spirals into a mess  of four sentimentalism and dated cgi  ravaged by critics and considered a box  office dud jackfrost is a movie many  teens enjoyed in the 1990s with their  families and then wisely consigned it to  the history books  runway hughes 1999 rom-com forces of  nature was poised for success even after  it was met with harsh reviews from  critics the movie follows writer ben  holmes as he treks back to his hometown  of savannah georgia for his wedding  ben's travel plans are appended when he  crosses paths with free-spirited offbeat  sarah on his flight before a seagull  flies into their plane's jet engine  grounding them when a brewing hurricane  leads all other flights to be cancelled  ben and sarah are forced to team up and  find an alternate path south leading to  a screwball journey that leaves ben  questioning his commitment to his  fiancee even when ben and sarah's  hijinks veer into the cartoonish forces  of nature was a pleasant watch in the  late 1990s mostly due to ben affleck and  sandra bullock's shia star power but the  movie is rarely discussed this side of  the 21st century likely due to a  forgettable plot and sarah's passe manic  pixie dream girl characterization this  is a film that was simply never destined  to leave the 90s  following in the colossal footsteps of  jurassic park and godzilla lake placid  took a stab at the monster genre and by  most accounts missed by a long shot  still the bizarre concept of an enormous  30-foot saltwater crocodile terrorizing  a lake in upstate new york managed to  drive curious audiences to the theaters  despite a wickedly hilarious supporting  performance delivered by the late great  betty white this creature features goofy  thrills wore off quickly it is virtually  impossible to recall anything that's  happened in the movie apart from the  infamous scene in which white leaves a  blindfolded cow to be consumed in a  single vicious chomp  this is due to a heavy reliance on flat  b-movie characterization aimless  plotting and the cheesy scripts that was  inexplicably written by david e kelly  one of the most celebrated writers in  television drive me crazy is a prime  example of how a movie can be forgotten  when another one does the same plot but  better named after the 1999 britney  spears song featured on its soundtrack  this melissa jonehart and adrian grenier  starring romantic comedy was released  eight months after she's all that a  movie that was much better and more  successful drive me crazy never escaped  his competitor's shadow hart was at the  height of her popularity right in the  middle of her run on sabrina the teenage  witch but this was grenier's mainstream  breakthrough having only starred in a  handful of small independent films  although drive me crazy fed worse with  critics she's all that was never exactly  bound for the criterion collection the  latter employs the same trite ugly  duckling gets a makeover conceders drive  me crazy but with better chemistry  between the leads which really makes or  breaks these kinds of movies she's all  that basically obliterated drive me  crazy from the 1990s teen rom-com cannon  and even went on to inspire a  genderflipped netflix remake in 2021  james foley's 1996 stalker drama fear  was a provocative must see among teens  at the time but today it's cringe  inducing dialogue and nonsensical plot  reeks of unintended camp characterized  by one of its producers as fatal  attraction for teens the psychological  thriller stars mark woolberg as  mysterious bad boy david and depicts the  toxic relationship he pursues with his  younger girlfriend nicole once nicole's  father digs into david's past and  discovers david is not the person he  claims to be he tries to persuade his  daughter to end things only stoking  david's troubling timber in fairness  wolberg delivers a truly chilling  performance as david develops his  unhealthy obsession with nicole and his  character's volatility was amusing to  watch as a teenager today though it is  difficult to enjoy fear even as a hate  watch mostly due to its glimped  portrayal of psychological and physical  abuse  saturday night live movie spin-offs do  not have the strongest track record  bruce mccullough's 1999 movie superstar  included molly shannon's catholic school  girl mary catherine gallagher remains  one of snl's most beloved recurring  characters short comedy sketches proved  to be the ideal forum for shannon to  play mary catherine giving her the space  to tap into the character's  unpredictable intensity of putting  social awkwardness and physical comedy i  guess that's a catholic thing  expanding shannon's character into a  full-length feature heroine movie proved  challenging however forcing superstar to  rely on long drawn out sight gags that  often suffocate the movie's pacing  teenagers in the 1990s often mimicked  mary catherine's sticks and catchphrases  but these are all prime examples of  things that are best left in the late  1990s along with the movie itself  after writing the screenplays for some  of the most popular teen slasher movies  from the 1990s kevin williamson was  riding a huge wave of acclaim and  expectation for his directorial debut  williamson returned to a screenplay he  had written prior to his rapid ascent to  fame teaching mrs tingle this black  comedy follows high school student lee  ann as she enlists her friends to hold  reviled teacher mrs tingle hostage after  she gave the annapol grade on a project  and threatened to dethrone her status as  class valedictorian  the dark premise piqued the interest of  every teenager who dreamt of seeking  revenge on a mean teacher from high  school but considering the rise in  school violence since its release  teaching mrs tingle now feels in poor  taste there was also an undeniable  novelty in seeing a revered actress like  helen mirren partaking something so low  brow  but saddled with a schlocky script and  ghastly reviews teaching mrs tingle was  always doomed to be a one-and-done  based on two stories by the science  fiction literary master isaac asimov  chris columbus's 1999 fantasy drama  bicentennial man stars the late robin  williams who truly disappears into his  role as andrew martin a robotic domestic  worker who yearns to become a human  being however what starts out with a  charming fish out of water story quickly  dissolves into modern existentialism as  andrew discovers the limits of his  ability to emulate human feelings the  movie struggles to understand what it  wants to communicate to its audience  employing increasingly emotionally  manipulative tactics to entertain  children and emotionally stir adults  critics were mostly mixed from the film  and the box office numbers were not  encouraging few actors have enjoyed as  much consistent success as williams in  the 1990s but bicentennial man is too  much of a bummer to deserve a second  viewing which is why when it comes to  william's best work it is perennially  absent from the conversation  inspired by the classic fairy tale  little red riding hood writer and  director matthew bright's freeway  featured a breakthrough performance from  rhys witherspoon one that kicked off her  long and successful career with the  spoon stars as vanessa a troubled  teenager and little red riding hood  surrogate who is left alone to fend for  herself after her mother is arrested she  evades a social worker trying to help  her and goes on the run to track down  her elusive grandmother unwittingly  hitching a ride with a wanted serial  killer the trip quickly descends into  chaos leading vanessa to commit heinous  acts of violence in order to survive  freeway was favored by critics and  audiences alike but never garnered the  level of fandom needed to catapult it  into cult movie territory the gritty  road comedy thriller felt edgy and  audacious when it debuted at the 1996  sundance film festival  firt feels antiquated by today's  standards and has since virtually  disappeared from public consciousness  [Music]
 

